MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An interrupt IN transfer kept its channel while the endpoint NAKed,
waiting for its next interval. A hub's status endpoint and the
notification endpoint of every CDC ACM function are always pending: with
a hub and four such devices behind it, they hold most of the controller's
channels (8 on the ESP32-S3) without moving any data, and control and OUT
transfers wait for one of them to complete.

When the endpoint NAKs, park the transfer: give the channel back, leave
the transfer queued with its schedule kept in the endpoint state, and
take a channel again one frame before the next poll. A later transfer of
the same endpoint waits behind the parked one, and the endpoint's
transfers move to the end of the queue, behind those of the other
endpoints. A parked transfer that is cancelled is returned at once.

