Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:13:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] drivers: usb: uhc_dwc2: give a NAKing bulk IN channel
 to waiting transfers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The core retries a bulk IN transaction the device NAKs, so a bulk IN
transfer keeps its channel until data arrives. A host reading the
console of a quiet CDC ACM device holds a channel per device that way,
and with more such endpoints than channels the transfers queued behind
them, control transfers included, wait until one of the devices sends
something.

When transfers wait for a channel, unmask NAK on the bulk IN channels.
On the next NAK, halt the channel and park the transfer: keep what was
received and the data toggle, give the channel back and resume the
transfer later, behind the transfers of the other endpoints. A NAK that
comes when nothing waits any more only masks NAK again.

Assisted-by: Claude:opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Benjamin Cabé <benjamin@zephyrproject.org>
